CPM-9 canonical numbers (FINAL, frozen 2026-05-18)
=====================================================

Universe: 9 risky ETFs (DBMF dropped after year-by-year validation)
  US (4):           QQQ, IWF (live: SCHG), VBR, SPHQ
  International (2): EFA, EEM            # iShares, older history vs VEA/VWO
  Diversifiers (3): GLD, TLT, DBC (live: PDBC)

Engine: TOP_K_CANDIDATES=5, HOLD_BUFFER=2.5z, CORR_LOOKBACK=756d (~3y)
Cost: 10bps/side, MaxLeverage=1.0 (de-risk only), TargetVol=10%
Blend: 70% CPM + 30% BULL-QQQ

Canonical window: 2007-02-28 -> 2026-05 (19.2y)
  All 9 RISKY ETFs LIVE at window start (DBC live 2006-02 + 12mo signal warmup).
  Only HYG (canary) uses VWEHX mutual-fund stitch pre-2007-04-04 (existing
  established proxy, not contamination of risky pair-selection candidate pool).
  Includes full 2008 GFC realization (CPM standalone -13.4% MaxDD).

Live-trade ticker mapping:
  IWF -> SCHG     (Schwab US Large Growth, 14bps cheaper, corr 0.994)
  DBC -> PDBC     (no K-1, smarter optimum-yield roll, corr 0.956)
  All others same.

Why DBMF was dropped (2026-05-18):
  Year-by-year analysis of post-2020 (DBMF-warmup) window:
    2020: DBMF added 0.00% (not selected)
    2021: DBMF added 0.00% (not selected)
    2022: DBMF added -0.02% (the supposed crisis year -- ZERO benefit)
    2023: DBMF added -0.31% (drag in reversal)
    2024: DBMF added +8.44% (entire MF case rests here)
    2025: DBMF added -0.02% (not selected)
    2026 YTD: DBMF added -0.15%
  Single-year (2024) dependency + 7y live sample = too much DSR risk.
  -0.04 Sh canonical cost from drop = within bootstrap 95% CI [0.91, 1.82].
  KMLM tested as alternative -- live-only KMLM gives identical numbers to
  live-only DBMF; pre-2020 KMLM stitch (MLM Index 1988+) hurts more.

